{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And YHWH struck every firstborn in the land of Egypt.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, repaid them measure for measure with these ten plagues, and therefore the plagues were דצ\"ך עד\"ש באח\"ב. Their mainstay of trust was the Nile, which watered their fields and vineyards, and they subjugated Israel to draw its waters; therefore the waters of the Nile turned to blood. They would rouse Israel from their sleep and rouse them from their beds at night for crushing labor, and they would scream from the burden — because of the pain of the heart He brought upon them frogs in their chambers and upon their beds, as it says ״ובחדר משכבך ועל מטתך״, and the frogs would croak in their innards. They withheld bathhouses from Israel and the lice afflicted them; therefore their earth swarmed with lice. They would set traps for them to hunt beasts such as lions and bears for us; therefore He brought upon them wild beasts (ערוב). They would subjugate them to tend their livestock; therefore He sent among them pestilence (דבר). They would subjugate them to heat water for them; He brought upon them boils (שחין). They would stone them with stones; He brought upon them hail (ברד). They would decree upon them, since they were vintners in their vineyards, to bring upon them locusts (ארבה) to destroy the fruit. They would lock them in the house of the imprisoned, in prisons and in dark places; He brought upon them darkness (חשך). They plotted to kill Israel, who are called the firstborn of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it says (Exodus 4:22) ״בני בכורי ישראל״; therefore He killed their firstborn. This is what is written: ״וה' הכה כל בכור״." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Let the name of the King of kings of kings, the Holy One, blessed be He, be praised, who brought the plagues upon Pharaoh and his army according to the royal stratagem (כטכסיס המלכים), for so is the way of a king of flesh and blood who comes to wage war against another king: first he cuts off their water — so the Holy One, blessed be He, did at first: He dammed their water channel by turning their waters to blood, and they would die of thirst; this is what it says: ״כי לא יכלו לשתות ממימי היאור״. And afterwards he brings against them trumpeters and rattling troops with great noise, with the neighing of horses and chariots, as it is written (Nahum 3:2) ״סוס דוהר ומרכבה מרקדה״, terrifying the heart and making a man's innards cry out from the magnitude of the fear; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought upon them frogs, which would whistle and emit sound. Afterwards he brings against them archers to shoot arrows at them; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought upon them lice, which would enter their bodies like a kind of arrow. Afterwards he adds and sends peoples, many from distant lands and foreign tongues; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought upon them wild beasts (ערוב), and they are wild beasts of the wilderness in many diverse species to destroy everything. And afterwards he draws closer and sends (דורמסאות — the meaning: he sends horsemen to run around the land to kill the livestock); so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought pestilence (דבר) upon their livestock. And afterwards he draws closer and brings naphta to kill the ambushing troops; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought upon them boils (שחין). And afterwards he draws closer and brings and hurls against them catapult stones to breach the city walls; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought hail (ברד). And afterwards the multitudes and troops gather to enter the city; so the Holy One, blessed be He, did — He brought upon them locusts (ארבה), which would strike and destroy everything the hail had left. Once they entered, they seized the people of the city and put them in the house of the imprisoned — this is the darkness (חשך). And afterwards He struck all their great ones, as it says: ״ומת כל בכור בארץ מצרים״. And all the plagues that the Holy One, blessed be He, brought upon the Egyptians in Egypt, He is destined to bring upon Edom, as it says (Isaiah 23:5) ״כאשר שמע למצרים יחילו כשמע צר״ — every צר lacking the letter ו referenced in Scripture speaks of the kingdom of Edom. In Egypt — blood, and in Edom — blood, as it says (Joel 3:3) ״דם ואש ותמרות עשן״. In Egypt — frogs: their voice was heard; and in Edom it is written (Isaiah 66:6) ״קול שאון מעיר קול מהיכל״. In Egypt — her dust turned to lice; and in Edom it is written (ibid. 34) ״ונהפכו נחליה לזפת ועפרה לגפרית״. In Egypt — wild beasts (ערוב); and in Edom it is written (ibid. 11) ״וירשוה קאת וקפד וינשוף ועורב וגו׳״. In Egypt — pestilence (דבר); and in Edom it is written (Ezekiel 38:22) ״ונשפטתי אתו בדבר ובדם״. In Egypt — boils (שחין); and in Edom it is written (Zechariah 14:12) ״המק בשרו והוא עומד על רגליו״. In Egypt — hail (ברד); and in Edom it is written (Ezekiel 13:13) ״ואבני אלגביש״. In Egypt — locusts (ארבה); and in Edom it is written (ibid. 39) ״בן אדם אמור לצפור כל כנף הקבצו ובאו״. In Egypt — darkness (חשך); and in Edom it is written (Isaiah 34:11) ״ונטה עליה קו תהו ואבני בהו״. In Egypt — the plague of the firstborn; and in Edom it is written (ibid.) ״כי רותה בשמים חרבי הנה על אדום תרד ועל עם חרמי למשפט״, and it is written (ibid.) ״חרב לה' מלאה דם הדשנה מחלב״, and it is written (ibid.) ״כי זבח לה' בבצרה וגו׳״, and it is written (ibid.) ״וירדו ראמים עמהם״. Rabbi Meir says: these are the Romans. Rabbi Abba bar Kahana says: darkness and gloom served in Egypt, but תהו ובהו did not serve in this world, and they are destined to serve in the great metropolis of Rome, as it says (ibid.) ״ונטה עליה קו תהו ואבני בהו״ — for the nations of the world who did not accept the Torah, out of the darkness, as it is said of them (ibid. 60) ״כי הנה החשך יכסה ארץ וערפל לאומים״, and concerning Israel it is said (ibid.) ״ועליך יזרח ה' וכבודו עליך יראה״. He who punished the former ones will punish the latter ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:33.548511092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}